  "final_text": "Kartovka in Brno (offer C) is the cheapest once delivery and the payment discount are counted: **€24,910 a year**, which is €962 less than Rednitz in Nürnberg (A). Wartapak in Poznań (B) has the lowest price per box but comes out most expensive. These figures assume 40,000 boxes a year delivered to Rampe 3, as stated in your request, and were calculated in code.\n\n| Line | A · Rednitz, Nürnberg | B · Wartapak, Poznań | C · Kartovka, Brno |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Goods** | 40,000 × €0.66 = **€26,400** (A l.16) | €520 per 1,000 → €0.52 × 40,000 = **€20,800** (B l.13) | €57.50 per 100 → €0.575 × 40,000 = **€23,000** (C l.15) |\n| **Freight** | **€0**, supplier delivers to your door (DAP) (A l.21) | They don't deliver (EXW). Minimum order 20,000 = 2 trucks × €1,400 = **€2,800** (B l.14, l.16; kosten-intern l.16) | They don't deliver (FCA). 10,000 per delivery = 4 trips × €650 = **€2,600** (C l.17–18; kosten-intern l.17) |\n| **One-off** | **€0**, die and printing plate free (A l.19) | Die **€1,450** (B footnote l.21) | **€0** (C l.11) |\n| **Storage** | **€0**: you can order from 3,000 at a time, so ≤10 pallets fit in your own space (A l.22; kosten-intern l.8) | 20 pallets − 10 = 10 places × €16 × 12 months = **€1,920** (kosten-intern l.7–10) | 10 pallets − 10 = **€0** |\n| **Discount** | 2% of goods = **−€528** (A l.24) | 2% of goods only = **−€416**. The die gets no discount (B l.17, l.22) | 3% of goods = **−€690** (C l.19) |\n| **Total** | **€25,872** | **€26,554** | **€24,910** |\n\n**Result:** Brno costs €962 less than Nürnberg and €1,644 less than Poznań. Freight decides it: Brno's goods are €3,400 cheaper than Nürnberg's, but €2,600 of that goes on transport. Poznań's €5,600 lead on goods is used up by freight, the die and external storage.\n\n**Things that could change the order:**\n- **Brno's paper surcharge (C l.22–24):** If the paper index rises between order and delivery, Brno adds 60% of the goods value times the rise, and no discount applies to it. At about **7.0%** (60% × €23,000 × 7% ≈ €962), Nürnberg becomes cheaper. Nürnberg's price is fixed until 31 Dec 2027 (A l.26). The index will only be named in Brno's order confirmation, so you can't see your exposure in advance.\n- **Offer deadlines:** Brno's offer is valid for 30 days from 16 Oct, so until about **15 Nov 2026**. Poznań's runs until 30 Nov 2026. Both end before the contract starts in January 2027, so their prices for 2027 aren't confirmed.\n- **Nürnberg's volume price of €0.62 (A l.17)** starts at 60,000 boxes. I didn't use it because you're ordering 40,000.\n\n**Open questions:**\n- **Poznań:** Can a 20,000-box order be delivered in several smaller loads? That would remove the €1,920 for external storage, but Poznań would still be €682 behind Nürnberg.\n- **Annual volume:** Does it stay at 40,000? Fewer boxes mostly hurt Poznań, which has the €1,450 die cost and the 20,000-box minimum order.\n\nThe table shows what each offer costs; choosing a supplier is your call.",
